@*
    ── Lecturer Home (Dashboard) ────────────────────────────────────────────
    Data source:   IDashboardOverviewService.GetAsync("lecturer")
                   IProjectRequestsService.GetAllAsync()
                   IPendingMentorApprovalsService.GetPendingAsync()

    ── THREE QUESTIONS, THREE SURFACES ──────────────────────────────────────
      1. דורש פעולה           what the SYSTEM is waiting on me for, right now
      2. תמונת מצב צוותים      how are the teams IN THE COURSE — all of them
      3. מועדים קרובים         which academic dates are coming
      4. משימות אישיות         what I set myself

    THE LECTURER HOLDS TWO ROLES AT ONCE and the middle surface is where that
    used to go wrong. This page previously carried "הצוותים בהנחייתי" — a list
    of the teams the reader personally mentors — which made Home a SUPERVISOR's
    dashboard with course facts arranged around it. It also did not scale: a
    lecturer with fifteen supervised teams got הצוותים שלי rebuilt inside a
    card that can show four rows.

    ── THE VOCABULARY, AND IT MUST NOT BLEED ────────────────────────────────
      דורש פעולה        an entity whose CURRENT WORKFLOW STATE requires this
                        role to act. Never a to-do, never something a person
                        marks done.
      תמונת מצב צוותים   course-wide awareness across EVERY team in the cycle.
                        Its question is "where should I look", not "what do I
                        owe".
      בהנחייתי           a CONTEXT inside that population — a count in the
                        summary line and a tag on a row. Never the card's
                        scope.
      מועדים קרובים      future academic dates. Not work items, and never
                        sorted or coloured as if they were.
      שיבוצים            owns mentor-assignment problems ("ללא מנחה משויך").
                        That metric was on this page and has been removed:
                        a team with no mentor is an assignment failure, and
                        Home is not where assignment is done.

    ── דורש פעולה IS A SYSTEM WORK QUEUE, NOT A TODO LIST ───────────────────
    Every row is an ENTITY whose own state currently requires this role.
    Nothing is created, stored, checked off or completed here:

      בקשה   ProjectRequests row whose Status is owned by staff
             (RequestOwnership.AwaitsStaff) → /management/requests?open=N
      הגשה   TaskSubmissions row with MentorStatus = 'Pending'
             → /lecturer/submissions?open=N

    Both are LIVE QUERIES over the real tables — `WHERE s.MentorStatus =
    'Pending'` and the request's own Status column. There is no work-item
    table, no mirrored row and no second copy of any state. An item leaves the
    queue the moment the underlying entity moves: the mentor approves or the
    lecturer override-approves and MentorStatus stops being 'Pending'; the
    request is resolved, closed or handed back and its Status stops being
    staff-owned. A returned submission that is resubmitted becomes 'Pending'
    again and reappears by itself. Nothing on this page has to be told.

    A CLICK OPENS THE ENTITY — not a preview, not a task-detail panel. The row
    is an anchor into the module that can actually change the item's state.

    ── TWO KINDS OF WORK, TWO CARDS ─────────────────────────────────────────
    Home also carries the lecturer's OWN reminders — PersonalTasks rows, the
    existing table keyed on UserId with an IsDone column. That is what let
    "המשימות שלי" be retired as a DESTINATION: the system feeds that page
    showed were already here, and its one irreplaceable feature was somewhere to
    jot "check the scope with team 4".

    They spent one pass inside דורש פעולה and have their own card now, because
    the two are not the same concept and one list cannot honestly hold both:

      בקשה / הגשה   THE SYSTEM IS WAITING ON YOU. Completion comes from the
                    WORKFLOW — no checkbox, ever. The row is an anchor into the
                    module that owns the entity, and it disappears when that
                    entity's own state moves.
      משימה          YOU ARE WAITING ON YOURSELF. Completion comes from the
                    PERSON, through PATCH …/personal-tasks/{id}/toggle — the
                    same endpoint /lecturer/tasks and the calendar call.

    Mixing them put two kinds of completion in one list and made the queue's
    count — the number the header sentence quotes — a figure about two unrelated
    things. Separated, "N פריטים ממתינים לפעולתך" means only what it says, and
    the reminder count sits on the card that owns it.

    NO SECOND TASK SYSTEM, and none was created when they moved. Create, edit,
    complete and delete all go through IPersonalTasksService and
    MentorPersonalTaskModal — the same service and the same editor
    /lecturer/tasks, /mentor/tasks, /mentor/calendar and /lecturer/calendar
    already use. This page adds no model, no endpoint and no persistence, and
    there is still no tasks PAGE: Home is the surface, which is why that card
    links nowhere.

    מועדים קרובים refuses them too: it answers "what is coming academically",
    and a personal reminder is work, not a course date.

    ── THREE SURFACES, NOT FOUR ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    A fourth card, "מבט על הקורס", stood in the rail carrying total teams,
    teams needing attention and teams with no mentor. The first two are now the
    summary line inside תמונת מצב צוותים and the third has left the product's
    Home entirely, so the card had nothing left that was not said better
    somewhere else. It is removed rather than refilled — see the note above
    CourseSummary.

    ── ROSE IS EARNED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Waiting ages ride MentorAttention's single 3-day threshold, which never
    returns rose: neither a request nor a mentor approval has a deadline it
    could be late for. The only rose on this page is a team the server scored
    AtRisk.
*@
@page "/dashboard/lecturer"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff + "," + Roles.Mentor)]
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IDashboardOverviewService DashboardService
@inject IProjectRequestsService RequestsService
@inject IPendingMentorApprovalsService ApprovalsService
@inject IPersonalTasksService PersonalTasks

<div class="mdash-page" dir="rtl">

    @* ── Title row — THE GREETING, AND NOTHING ELSE ──
         It carried "N פריטים ממתינים לפעולתך" beside the name. That number is
         the work queue's own size, and the queue prints it on its "הכל" tab a
         few hundred pixels below — so the header was answering a question the
         reader was about to have answered properly, with rows under it.

         NOTHING REPLACED IT. The temptation is to put a different count here;
         every count worth having already sits on the thing it counts (the
         queue's tabs, the team snapshot's summary line, the personal card's
         bubble), so the honest result is a shorter header. *@
    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Hero"
                 Class="mdash-header"
                 Title="@_greeting" />

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת נתונים…" />
    }
    else if (_loadError || _data is null)
    {
        <MEmptyState Title="שגיאה בטעינת הדשבורד"
                     Description="ייתכן שיש תקלת רשת זמנית. אפשר לנסות לרענן את הדף." />
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── THE COMPOSITION ──
             WIDE (1.75fr)   דורש פעולה · תמונת מצב צוותים
             RAIL (1fr)      מועדים קרובים · משימות אישיות

             Four cards, two per column. The team band spanned the full width
             while the rail held one short card — the only arrangement that was
             balanced when there were three surfaces. There are four now, and
             the fourth is short, so the rail can carry a pair and the two
             columns end near the same line without anything being stretched to
             get there.

             NOTHING IS FORCED TO MATCH. The grid starts its columns at the top
             and every card is its own content's height — there is no
             min-height, no stretch and no fill anywhere in this file. Balance
             here is a consequence of what went where. *@
        <div class="mdash-grid">

            @* ── The wide column — what the system and the course need ── *@
            <div class="mdash-main-col">

            @* ── 1. דורש פעולה ──
                 THE PAGE'S ONE LIFTED CARD — the student dashboard's rule:
                 every other surface is quiet and exactly one carries the
                 emphasis, given to the card that answers "what needs me now".

                 Rows are MRow inside MRowList, and each renders as a real <a>
                 because each one goes somewhere real. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None"
                   Class="mdash-card-strong mdash-queue-card">
                @* THE ONE GLYPH ON THIS PAGE THAT IS NOT THE BRAND SWEEP.
                     Every other card head paints its mark with
                     #motivaIconGradient, which says "this is Motiva". This one
                     says something about the CONTENT instead: it is the only
                     head here whose card is about somebody being blocked on
                     this person. The student dashboard's attention card already
                     does exactly this (.orc-head-icon-rose) and this reads the
                     same token it does — see the stylesheet.

                     THE TONE STOPS AT THE GLYPH. The card keeps its white
                     surface and its brand-tinted lift; nothing else on it turns
                     red, because rose on this page has always meant one
                     specific thing and a red panel would spend it on the fact
                     that the card exists. `stroke="currentColor"` rather than a
                     second paint server — the colour is set once, in CSS. *@
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon mdash-head-icon-alert" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"></path>
                            <path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title mdash-queue-title">דורש פעולה</h2>

                    @* MFilterTabs — the control /lecturer/tasks already uses.
                       A LENS, not navigation: it hides rows the card already
                       holds and changes no feed, filter or count. A tab whose
                       count is zero renders no bubble. *@
                    @if (WorkQueue.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <div class="mdash-head-tabs">
                            <MFilterTabs Tabs="@FilterTabs"
                                         ActiveKey="@_filter"
                                         OnSelect="@(k => _filter = k)"
                                         AriaLabel="סינון תור העבודה" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>

                @if (WorkQueue.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MEmptyState Title="אין פריטים שממתינים לפעולה שלך."
                                 Description="בקשות והגשות שיגיעו למצב שדורש טיפול יופיעו כאן מעצמן. אפשר גם להוסיף משימה משלך." />
                }
                else if (VisibleQueue.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MEmptyState Title="אין פריטים בסינון הזה."
                                 Description="אפשר לחזור ל״הכל״ כדי לראות את שאר התור." />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MRowList Class="mdash-queue-list" AriaLabel="פריטים שדורשים את פעולתך">
                        @foreach (var item in VisibleQueue.Take(QueuePreview))
                        {
                            var it = item;
                            <MRow Class="mdash-queue-row"
                                  Primary="@it.Title"
                                  Secondary="@it.Context"
                                  Href="@it.Href"
                                  AriaLabel="@($"{it.TypeLabel}: {it.Title}. {it.Context}. {it.Wait}. {it.ActionLabel}")">
                                <Leading>
                                    <MStatusBadge Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
                                                  Variant="@it.TypeVariant"
                                                  Text="@it.TypeLabel" />
                                </Leading>
                                <Status>
                                    @* ── THE WAITING AGE IS A TAG ──────────
                                       It is a STATE of the item, not a fact
                                       about who owns it, and the context line
                                       is for ownership — team, mentor, request
                                       type. Buried mid-sentence it was the one
                                       thing on the row a lecturer scans for and
                                       could not find; in the row's end block it
                                       is scannable down the column.

                                       `.motiva-tag` is the product's ONE tag
                                       recipe — white paper under a gradient
                                       edge — and it is already on this very
                                       card, on the "בהנחייתי" subset marker.
                                       No new colour and no new shape: the type
                                       badge stays the row's only coloured
                                       chip, so the age never competes with the
                                       kind. Deliberately NOT rose at any age —
                                       a long wait is not a missed deadline, and
                                       neither a request nor a submission has
                                       one to miss. *@
                                    <span class="motiva-tag mdash-wait-tag">@it.Wait</span>
                                </Status>
                                <Trailing>
                                    @* The destination, said as the verb the
                                       lecturer will perform there.

                                       EVERY ROW ON THIS CARD ENDS THIS WAY, and
                                       that is the point: nothing here is
                                       completed in place, because nothing here
                                       belongs to this page. *@
                                    <span class="mdash-go">
                                        @it.ActionLabel
                                        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round"
                                             stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                            <path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </span>
                                </Trailing>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>

                }

                @* ── Where the rest of a long queue is reached ──
                     Conditional, because both destinations are in the nav
                     anyway: printing them beside a four-row queue that already
                     shows everything would be navigation for its own sake.

                     "+ משימה" HAS LEFT THIS BAR. It belonged to a card that
                     briefly held the lecturer's own items; that card is
                     משימות אישיות now, and the action went with them. *@
                @if (VisibleQueue.Count > QueuePreview)
                {
                    <div class="mdash-card-foot">
                        <a class="mdash-foot-link" href="management/requests">
                            לכל הבקשות
                            @if (RequestQueue.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="mdash-foot-n">@RequestQueue.Count</span>
                            }
                        </a>
                        <a class="mdash-foot-link" href="lecturer/submissions">
                            לכל ההגשות
                            @if (_pendingApprovals.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="mdash-foot-n">@_pendingApprovals.Count</span>
                            }
                        </a>
                    </div>
                }
            </MCard>

            @* ── 3. תמונת מצב צוותים ──
                 EVERY TEAM IN THE COURSE, and the answer to "where should I
                 look" rather than "what do I owe".

                 THE SUMMARY LINE IS THE WHOLE POPULATION. MSummaryTag is the
                 product's inert container for related counts — one box, a
                 hairline between facts, no hover, no cursor, no brand colour —
                 which is what keeps this from becoming three KPI tiles.
                 "בהנחייתי" appears there as CONTEXT: it tells the reader how
                 much of the course is personally theirs, and it does not
                 narrow anything on this card.

                 THE ROWS ARE EXCEPTIONS ONLY. Listing every team would rebuild
                 הצוותים שלי inside a card that can show three rows; listing
                 healthy teams to fill space would spend the dashboard's most
                 valuable rows on the teams that need nothing. So the preview is
                 the teams the SERVER already scored as needing attention, worst
                 first — and when there are none, the card says so in one line
                 instead of finding something to list. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-teams-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path>
                            <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle>
                            <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title">תמונת מצב צוותים</h2>
                    <div class="mdash-head-summary">
                        <MSummaryTag Metrics="@CourseSummary" />
                    </div>
                    <a class="sd-head-link" href="projects">לכל הצוותים</a>
                </div>

                @if (AttentionTeams.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-teams-calm">
                        <span class="mdash-teams-calm-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        אין כרגע צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב.
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    @* ── THE ROWS ARE AN EXCEPTION PREVIEW, AND THE CARD HAS
                         TO SAY SO ───────────────────────────────────────────
                         The card is course-wide — CourseTeams is every team in
                         the cycle and the summary line above counts all of
                         them — but the ROWS are only the teams the server
                         scored AtRisk or Attention. On a healthy cohort that
                         is one or two rows under a heading that says
                         "תמונת מצב צוותים", and it reads as though the
                         lecturer has one team.

                         A LINE, NOT A CARD AND NOT A SECOND LIST. The scope
                         was already derivable — the summary's third metric IS
                         this number — but derivable is not the same as
                         stated, and the fix for "the reader has to work it
                         out" is to say it, not to add a surface. "לכל הצוותים"
                         above is still the route to the whole population. *@
                    <p class="mdash-teams-scope">
                        מוצגים כאן רק הצוותים שדורשים תשומת לב —
                        @AttentionTeams.Count מתוך @CourseTeams.Count צוותים בקורס
                    </p>

                    <MRowList Class="mdash-team-list" AriaLabel="צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב">
                        @foreach (var t in AttentionTeams.Take(TeamsPreview))
                        {
                            <MRow Class="mdash-team-row"
                                  Primary="@t.TeamName"
                                  Secondary="@t.Context"
                                  Meta="@t.Reason"
                                  MetaTone="@t.ReasonTone"
                                  Href="@($"projects/{t.ProjectId}/overview")"
                                  AriaLabel="@($"מרחב הצוות {t.TeamName} — {t.Reason}")">
                                <Leading>
                                    @* Decorative: the row's own aria-label
                                       already names the state this dot
                                       encodes, and MStatusDot goes aria-hidden
                                       when given no AriaLabel — so the state is
                                       announced once. *@
                                    <MStatusDot Tone="@t.Tone" />
                                </Leading>
                                <Status>
                                    @if (t.IsMine)
                                    {
                                        @* CONTEXT, on a course-wide row: this
                                           one happens to be the reader's own.
                                           It marks a subset; it never filters
                                           the card. *@
                                        <span class="motiva-tag mdash-mine-tag">בהנחייתי</span>
                                    }
                                </Status>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>

                    @if (AttentionTeams.Count > TeamsPreview)
                    {
                        <p class="mdash-teams-more">
                            @MoreTeamsLabel(AttentionTeams.Count - TeamsPreview)
                        </p>
                    }
                }
            </MCard>

            </div>

            @* ── The rail — what is coming, and what the lecturer set
                 themselves. Both are short by construction, which is why they
                 pair: two compact cards beside two tall ones. *@
            <div class="mdash-side-col">

            @* ── 3. מועדים קרובים ──
                 A SMALL PREVIEW of what is coming academically — two or three
                 rows, never a calendar.

                 GROUPED BY DEADLINE. A cohort runs one programme, so the same
                 milestone falls on the same date for many projects at once;
                 ungrouped, this card printed "אפיון — Project A", "אפיון —
                 Project B" … and said one thing several times. One row per
                 (milestone, date) with the team count beside it says it once,
                 and a milestone that really does belong to one team still
                 names that team.

                 THE PRODUCT HAS NO MEETINGS. /lecturer/calendar composes its
                 month from this same milestone feed plus the lecturer's own
                 reminders, and the Google integration only PUSHES a reminder
                 out — it never reads events back. A meetings row would be
                 invented data, and personal reminders are deliberately not
                 used to pad this card either. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-dates-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="3"></rect>
                            <path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title" id="mdash-dates-h">מועדים קרובים</h2>
                    <a class="sd-head-link" href="lecturer/calendar">ליומן המלא</a>
                </div>

                @if (UpcomingItems.Count == 0)
                {
                    @* Two short lines and nothing else. An empty card must
                       collapse to the height of its message — see the
                       `.mdash-dates-empty` note in the stylesheet. *@
                    <p class="mdash-dates-empty">
                        <strong>אין מועדים קרובים</strong>
                        <span>המועד הבא יופיע כאן כשייקבע.</span>
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mdash-up-list">
                        @foreach (var u in UpcomingItems)
                        {
                            <a class="mdash-up-row @u.KindClass" href="@u.Href">
                                <span class="mdash-up-tile">
                                    <span class="mdash-up-day">@u.Date.Day.ToString("00")</span>
                                    <span class="mdash-up-month">@MotivaDates.ShortMonth(u.Date)</span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="mdash-up-body">
                                    <span class="mdash-up-title" title="@u.Label">@u.Label</span>
                                    <span class="mdash-up-meta">@u.When</span>
                                </span>
                            </a>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </MCard>


            @* ── 4. משימות אישיות ──
                 THE LECTURER'S OWN REMINDERS, and a different concept from
                 דורש פעולה — which is why it is a different card.

                 THE CARD IS NOT CALLED המשימות שלי, and the difference is not
                 cosmetic: that was the name of the PAGE this replaced, and a
                 possessive says "the place where your things live" — which is
                 exactly the destination the lecturer no longer has. משימות
                 אישיות names the KIND of item instead, which is what separates
                 it from דורש פעולה: not whose it is, but who created it.

                 They were briefly rows inside the work queue. That queue means
                 "the system is waiting on you", and a note you wrote yourself
                 is not the system waiting on anything: mixing them put two
                 kinds of completion in one list (a workflow moving elsewhere,
                 and a person ticking a box) and made the queue's count a number
                 about two unrelated things.

                 NOTHING ABOUT THE FUNCTIONALITY CHANGED IN THE MOVE. Same
                 IPersonalTasksService, same MentorPersonalTaskModal, same
                 toggle endpoint, same rows, same editor — this is a different
                 place to draw them, not a different implementation. There is
                 still no separate tasks PAGE: Home is the lecturer's
                 personal-task surface, which is why this card links nowhere. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-tasks-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"></path>
                            <path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title">משימות אישיות</h2>
                    @if (ActiveTasks.Count > 0)
                    {
                        @* The count lives HERE, on the card that owns it —
                           never folded into the header sentence, which is
                           about what the system is waiting for. *@
                        <span class="motiva-count mdash-head-count"
                              aria-label="@($"{ActiveTasks.Count} משימות פתוחות")">@ActiveTasks.Count</span>
                    }
                </div>

                @if (ActiveTasks.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-tasks-calm">
                        <span class="mdash-tasks-calm-mark" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
                        הכול בוצע
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MRowList Class="mdash-tasks-list" AriaLabel="משימות אישיות">
                        @foreach (var t in ActiveTasks.Take(TasksPreview))
                        {
                            var task = t;
                            @* A <div> row: MRow renders one when given neither
                               Href nor OnClick, which is what lets it hold two
                               real controls — the completion circle and a title
                               button — without nesting a button in a button. *@
                            <MRow Class="mdash-task-row"
                                  Secondary="@DueLabel(task)"
                                  MetaTone="MRow.RowMetaTone.Default">
                                <Leading>
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="mdash-check"
                                            disabled="@(_togglingId == task.Id)"
                                            @onclick="@(() => ToggleTaskAsync(task))"
                                            aria-label="@($"סימון \"{task.Title}\" כהושלמה")">
                                        <span class="mdash-check-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                    </button>
                                </Leading>
                                <PrimaryContent>
                                    <button type="button" class="mdash-task-title"
                                            @onclick="@(() => _editingTask = task)"
                                            title="@task.Title"
                                            aria-label="@($"עריכת המשימה {task.Title}")">@task.Title</button>
                                </PrimaryContent>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>

                    @if (ActiveTasks.Count > TasksPreview)
                    {
                        @* A FACT, not a link. There is nowhere to send the
                           reader — /lecturer/tasks is deliberately unlinked and
                           is not coming back as a destination — so this says
                           how many are held back and stops. *@
                        <p class="mdash-tasks-more">@MoreTasksLabel(ActiveTasks.Count - TasksPreview)</p>
                    }
                }

                <div class="mdash-card-foot">
                    <button type="button" class="mdash-add" @onclick="OpenNewTask">
                        <span class="mdash-add-glyph" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                        <span>משימה</span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </MCard>

            </div>

        </div>
    }

</div>

@* ── The lecturer's own item: create / edit / delete ──
     THE SHARED EDITOR, NOT A COPY. /lecturer/tasks, /mentor/tasks,
     /mentor/calendar and /lecturer/calendar all open this very component, so
     there is one set of validation rules, one delete confirmation and one
     Google-Calendar story rather than a second form on Home.

     `Projects` is left at its default empty list, which is correct for this
     role rather than a shortcut: the server grants a personal task a ProjectId
     only through ProjectMentors (CreatePersonalTask rejects it otherwise), and
     the modal already omits the whole project row when the list is empty — so
     a lecturer is shown exactly the fields they can actually use. *@
<MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@(_creatingTask || _editingTask is not null)"
                         EditingTask="@_editingTask"
                         OnClose="CloseTaskEditor"
                         OnSaved="OnTaskSaved"
                         OnDeleted="OnTaskDeleted" />

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    // ── Preview depths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Both lists are PREVIEWS handing off to the module that owns them, and the
    // caps are MEASURED rather than picked: greeting (64px) + queue + gap +
    // team band + page tail has to land inside the ~800px a 900px window leaves
    // after the shell's own chrome. At the base density a row costs ~67px, so
    // four and three fit with the queue's foot showing and three exception rows
    // present; five did not.
    //
    // The queue keeps the larger share because it is the page's primary card,
    // and its DEPTH is still visible without spending rows on it — the foot's
    // two links carry the full counts ("לכל הבקשות 7"). The exception list is
    // deliberately the shorter of the two: a course with many teams in trouble
    // is a reason to open /projects, not a reason to grow a dashboard card.
    private const int QueuePreview = 4;
    private const int TeamsPreview = 3;

    /// <summary>How many milestone groups מועדים קרובים shows. Three: it is a
    /// preview of the calendar, and the calendar is one click away.</summary>
    private const int UpcomingPreview = 3;

    /// <summary>How many reminders משימות אישיות shows. Four — the rail's two
    /// cards together have to stay shorter than the wide column's two, and this
    /// card is the one that can grow without limit. The rest are counted, not
    /// listed: there is nowhere to send the reader, since Home IS the
    /// personal-task surface now.</summary>
    private const int TasksPreview = 4;

    private DashboardOverviewDto?             _data;
    private List<ProjectRequestRowDto>        _requests         = new();
    private List<PendingMentorApprovalRowDto> _pendingApprovals = new();
    private List<PersonalTaskDto>             _personalTasks    = new();
    private bool _loading = true;
    private bool _loadError;

    /// <summary>The reminder open in the shared editor, or null. Doubles as the
    /// modal's IsOpen, which is MentorPersonalTaskModal's own contract on every
    /// other screen that opens it.</summary>
    private PersonalTaskDto? _editingTask;

    /// <summary>True while the editor is open on a NEW task — the same field
    /// cannot express "creating" and "editing nothing", so this does.</summary>
    private bool _creatingTask;

    /// <summary>The row whose toggle is in flight, so it cannot be pressed
    /// twice while the PATCH is on the wire.</summary>
    private int? _togglingId;

    /// <summary>The queue's lens: "" for everything, "submissions", "requests".
    /// Presentational only — it hides rows the card already holds and touches
    /// no feed, filter or count.</summary>
    private string _filter = "";

    // ── Time / greeting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string _greeting
    {
        get
        {
            var name = _user?.FirstName?.Trim();
            var hour = DateTime.Now.Hour;
            var part = hour < 12 ? "בוקר טוב"
                     : hour < 17 ? "צהריים טובים"
                     : hour < 21 ? "ערב טוב"
                     :             "לילה טוב";
            return string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) ? part : $"{part}, {name}";
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Three independent GETs, every one an endpoint this role was already
    /// authorised for and this page (or /lecturer/tasks) already called.
    /// Nothing was added to the server for this screen.
    ///
    /// <para>The two queue feeds are best-effort and fail to empty: one feed
    /// being down thins the queue rather than failing the page. Only the
    /// dashboard payload can render the error state, because both the team
    /// snapshot and the dates come from it.</para></summary>
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var overviewTask  = DashboardService.GetAsync("lecturer");
        var requestsTask  = SafeAsync(() => RequestsService.GetAllAsync());
        var approvalsTask = SafeAsync(() => ApprovalsService.GetPendingAsync());
        // An `async` lambda so the result type is inferred from the guard's own
        // nullable target: GetAsync answers a non-null list, and returning it
        // straight from a non-async lambda is a variance mismatch the compiler
        // reports (CS8619) even though the value can never be null.
        var personalTask  = SafeAsync<PersonalTaskDto>(async () => await PersonalTasks.GetAsync());

        await Task.WhenAll(overviewTask, requestsTask, approvalsTask, personalTask);

        _data             = await overviewTask;
        _loadError        = _data is null;
        _requests         = await requestsTask;
        _pendingApprovals = await approvalsTask;
        _personalTasks    = await personalTask;

        _loading = false;
    }

    /// <summary>Await a feed, answering an empty list instead of throwing. The
    /// services already swallow transport failures and answer null; this folds
    /// the null in so every call site below can assume a list.</summary>
    /// <summary>One guard for every feed. A service that already answers a
    /// non-null list (IPersonalTasksService.GetAsync swallows its own transport
    /// failure) satisfies this signature unchanged — nullability annotations are
    /// not part of the delegate's type, so a second overload for it would not
    /// even compile.</summary>
    private static async Task<List<T>> SafeAsync<T>(Func<Task<List<T>?>> call)
    {
        try   { return await call() ?? new List<T>(); }
        catch { return new List<T>(); }
    }

    // ── 1. דורש פעולה — the system work queue ────────────────────────────────

    private enum WorkKind { Submission, Request }

    /// <summary>One row. Every field is DERIVED from the entity's current state
    /// on each render — there is no stored work item, so there is nothing to
    /// keep in sync and nothing to mark done. <c>Href</c> and
    /// <c>ActionLabel</c> carry where the row goes and what is done there.
    ///
    /// <para>It briefly had a third kind and a <c>Payload</c> to carry the
    /// lecturer's own reminders. Both are gone with them: every row on this
    /// card is now an entity that is completed SOMEWHERE ELSE, which is what
    /// lets the record stay this small.</para></summary>
    /// <summary>One row of the queue.
    ///
    /// <para><c>Context</c> is OWNERSHIP — team, mentor, request type — and
    /// <c>Wait</c> is STATE. They are separate fields because they render in
    /// separate places: the context line under the title, and a tag in the
    /// row's end block. Neither ever repeats the other.</para></summary>
    private sealed record WorkItem(
        WorkKind Kind,
        string   TypeLabel,
        MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant TypeVariant,
        string   Title,
        string   Context,
        string   Wait,
        string   ActionLabel,
        string   Href,
        bool     IsEscalated,
        int      Age);

    /// <summary>
    /// Requests the ACADEMIC SIDE owes the next move on.
    ///
    /// <para>The filter is <c>RequestOwnership.AwaitsStaff</c> — the product's
    /// single answer to whose court a request is in — read here rather than
    /// restated. It is deliberately narrower than the "להחלטתך" tab on the
    /// requests screen, which is a broad queue and includes NeedsInfo: that
    /// status means the request was handed back to the STUDENT and is waiting
    /// on them. A lecturer cannot move it forward, so listing it in a work
    /// queue would be asking for an action that is not theirs to take.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>THIS IS ALSO HOW A ROW LEAVES. Resolve, close, hand back or send
    /// for a mentor recommendation, and the status stops satisfying the
    /// predicate — the row is simply not built on the next load. Nothing marks
    /// it complete.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<ProjectRequestRowDto> RequestQueue =>
        _requests
            .Where(r => RequestOwnership.AwaitsStaff(r.Status))
            .OrderBy(r => r.CreatedAt)
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>The two feeds as one ordered queue. Escalated first — a wait
    /// past the product's shared 3-day threshold — and longest-waiting first
    /// within each half.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<WorkItem> WorkQueue
    {
        get
        {
            var items = new List<WorkItem>();

            // GET /api/task-submissions/pending-mentor-approvals is literally
            // `WHERE s.MentorStatus = 'Pending'`. Approve it, or override-
            // approve it from the submissions screen, and the row stops being
            // returned.
            foreach (var a in _pendingApprovals)
            {
                items.Add(new WorkItem(
                    Kind:        WorkKind.Submission,
                    TypeLabel:   "הגשה",
                    // Info is the blue role inside .motiva-final — the same one
                    // MentorAttentionRows.TypeVariant gives a submission, so a
                    // submission is the same colour on both roles' screens.
                    TypeVariant: MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Info,
                    Title:       a.TaskTitle,
                    Context:     Join(OneOf(a.TeamName, a.ProjectTitle),
                                      MentorLabel(a.MentorName)),
                    Wait:        MentorAging.ShortLabel(a.DaysWaiting),
                    ActionLabel: "לבדיקה",
                    Href:        $"lecturer/submissions?open={a.SubmissionId}",
                    IsEscalated: MentorAttention.AgeOf(a.DaysWaiting) == MentorAttentionAge.NeedsAttention,
                    Age:         a.DaysWaiting));
            }

            foreach (var r in RequestQueue)
            {
                int days = DaysOpen(r);
                items.Add(new WorkItem(
                    Kind:        WorkKind.Request,
                    TypeLabel:   "בקשה",
                    TypeVariant: MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Violet,
                    Title:       r.Title,
                    Context:     Join(OneOf(r.TeamName, r.ProjectTitle),
                                      TypeName(r.RequestType)),
                    Wait:        MentorAging.ShortLabel(days),
                    ActionLabel: "להחלטה",
                    Href:        $"management/requests?open={r.Id}",
                    IsEscalated: MentorAttention.AgeOf(days) == MentorAttentionAge.NeedsAttention,
                    Age:         days));
            }

            return items
                .OrderByDescending(i => i.IsEscalated)
                .ThenByDescending(i => i.Age)
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    private IReadOnlyList<WorkItem> VisibleQueue => _filter switch
    {
        "requests"    => WorkQueue.Where(i => i.Kind == WorkKind.Request).ToList(),
        "submissions" => WorkQueue.Where(i => i.Kind == WorkKind.Submission).ToList(),
        _             => WorkQueue,
    };

    /// <summary>The lens, carrying each kind's size. A zero renders no bubble,
    /// which is MFilterTabs' own rule. The "משימות" tab left with the personal
    /// rows — a filter for a kind this card cannot contain is a promise it
    /// cannot keep.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MFilterTabs.Tab> FilterTabs => new[]
    {
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("",            "הכל",   WorkQueue.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("requests",    "בקשות", RequestQueue.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("submissions", "הגשות", _pendingApprovals.Count),
    };

    // ── 4. משימות אישיות — the lecturer's own items ──────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// ACTIVE reminders, soonest first.
    ///
    /// <para><c>IsDone</c> is the existing completion flag and a ticked reminder
    /// is finished work, so it simply leaves this list — completed tasks are not
    /// re-listed anywhere on Home. The order is LecturerTasksPage's own: by due
    /// date ascending with undated tasks last, which is what
    /// <c>DateTime.MaxValue</c> buys.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PersonalTaskDto> ActiveTasks =>
        _personalTasks
            .Where(t => !t.IsDone)
            .OrderBy(t => t.DueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
            .ThenByDescending(t => t.CreatedAt)
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>
    /// A reminder's one line: when it is due, and the project it belongs to
    /// when it has one.
    ///
    /// <para>The server populates ProjectTitle / TeamName only while the caller
    /// still mentors that project, so a task whose project the lecturer can no
    /// longer see shows its date alone rather than a stale name.</para></summary>
    private static string DueLabel(PersonalTaskDto t)
    {
        var where = OneOf(t.TeamName, t.ProjectTitle);
        if (t.DueDate is not { } due) return Join("ללא תאריך יעד", where);

        int days = (DateTime.Today - due.Date).Days;
        // "באיחור" is allowed HERE and nowhere else on this page: a reminder is
        // the only thing on Home carrying a date its owner chose, so it is the
        // only thing that can be late. A request and a submission have no
        // deadline to miss — see WaitingLabel.
        var when = days switch
        {
            > 1 => $"באיחור {days} ימים",
            1   => "באיחור יום",
            0   => "היום",
            -1  => "מחר",
            _   => $"עד {due:dd.MM}",
        };
        return Join(when, where);
    }

    // ── Create, complete, edit ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // ALL FOUR OPERATIONS ARE THE EXISTING ONES. IPersonalTasksService and
    // MentorPersonalTaskModal are what /lecturer/tasks, /mentor/tasks,
    // /mentor/calendar and /lecturer/calendar already use; this page adds no
    // model, no endpoint, no table and no second editor.

    private void OpenNewTask()
    {
        _editingTask  = null;
        _creatingTask = true;
    }

    private void CloseTaskEditor()
    {
        _editingTask  = null;
        _creatingTask = false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Complete (or un-complete) one reminder.
    ///
    /// <para>PATCH …/personal-tasks/{id}/toggle — the endpoint the tasks page
    /// and the calendar call, whose UPDATE carries <c>AND UserId = @@UserId</c>
    /// so ownership is structural rather than a check this page could get
    /// wrong.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>The flag is flipped locally afterwards rather than refetching four
    /// feeds to learn one bit; the row then fails the <c>!IsDone</c> filter and
    /// leaves the queue on the next render.</para></summary>
    private async Task ToggleTaskAsync(PersonalTaskDto task)
    {
        if (_togglingId is not null) return;

        _togglingId = task.Id;
        var ok = await PersonalTasks.ToggleAsync(task.Id);
        _togglingId = null;

        if (ok) task.IsDone = !task.IsDone;
    }

    /// <summary>A saved reminder is folded into the list in place — the modal
    /// has already written it, and this only keeps the queue in step.</summary>
    private void OnTaskSaved(PersonalTaskDto saved)
    {
        var hit = _personalTasks.FindIndex(t => t.Id == saved.Id);
        if (hit >= 0) _personalTasks[hit] = saved;
        else          _personalTasks.Add(saved);

        CloseTaskEditor();
    }

    private void OnTaskDeleted(int deletedId)
    {
        _personalTasks.RemoveAll(t => t.Id == deletedId);
        CloseTaskEditor();
    }

    // ── 2. תמונת מצב צוותים — course-wide ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// THE POPULATION: every team in the course.
    ///
    /// <para>The server's lecturer scope is every project in the current
    /// academic year with a published team assignment and a real status —
    /// which is exactly what /projects lists — so "in the course" means the
    /// same thing on both screens and the CTA lands on the same set.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<DashboardProjectRowDto> CourseTeams =>
        _data?.Projects ?? (IReadOnlyList<DashboardProjectRowDto>)Array.Empty<DashboardProjectRowDto>();

    /// <summary>
    /// The teams the SERVER already scored as needing attention, worst first.
    ///
    /// <para><b>No new health rule.</b> HealthBucket arrives on the row, derived
    /// server-side from HealthScore (100 minus weighted overdue tasks, missing
    /// submissions, stale open requests and an overdue current milestone). This
    /// reads the two buckets that are not Healthy and orders by the score
    /// itself — the same rule the previous lecturer dashboard's
    /// "צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב" card used, restored rather than
    /// reinvented.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>SUPERVISION DOES NOT NARROW THIS. A team in trouble is the
    /// lecturer's business whether or not they personally mentor it; whether
    /// they do is carried on the row as a tag.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<TeamItem> AttentionTeams =>
        CourseTeams
            .Where(p => p.HealthBucket is HealthBuckets.AtRisk or HealthBuckets.Attention)
            .OrderBy(p => p.HealthScore)
            .Select(BuildTeamItem)
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>
    /// The summary line — the whole population, in one inert container.
    ///
    /// <para>THIS IS WHAT REPLACED "מבט על הקורס". That card carried these same
    /// two counts plus "ללא מנחה משויך"; the counts belong beside the teams
    /// they describe, and the third has left Home entirely because a team with
    /// no assigned mentor is a שיבוצים problem and Assignments is the screen
    /// that owns it. Nothing was invented to keep a card alive.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Rejected for the same reason: the course-wide submission ratio
    /// (Charts.SubmissionsSubmitted / NotYet) does answer a different question,
    /// but it is a progress statistic with no action behind it on this page —
    /// a KPI, which is the one thing this dashboard is not.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MSummaryTag.Metric> CourseSummary => new[]
    {
        new MSummaryTag.Metric(CourseTeams.Count.ToString(), "צוותים בקורס"),
        new MSummaryTag.Metric(CourseTeams.Count(p => p.IsSupervisedByCurrentUser).ToString(), "בהנחייתי"),
        new MSummaryTag.Metric(AttentionTeams.Count.ToString(), "דורשים תשומת לב"),
    };

    private sealed record TeamItem(
        int ProjectId, string TeamName, string Context, string Reason,
        MStatusDot.DotTone Tone, MRow.RowMetaTone ReasonTone, bool IsMine);

    /// <summary>
    /// One exception row: who, whose team it is, and WHY it is on this list.
    ///
    /// <para>The reason is read off the counts the server already sent, in the
    /// same priority order הצוותים שלי uses — so a team reads the same on both
    /// screens. Rose is the AtRisk bucket only; Attention is ordinary work in
    /// flight and takes the brand tone.</para></summary>
    private static TeamItem BuildTeamItem(DashboardProjectRowDto p)
    {
        bool atRisk = p.HealthBucket == HealthBuckets.AtRisk;

        string reason =
            p.OverdueTaskCount       > 0 ? $"{p.OverdueTaskCount} משימות באיחור"
          : p.MissingSubmissionCount > 0 ? "הגשה ממתינה לאישור"
          : p.OpenRequestCount       > 0 ? "בקשה פתוחה"
          :                                 HealthBuckets.Label(p.HealthBucket);

        // Project, current stage and the mentor — "where should I look" is
        // answered by knowing whose team this is and how far along it is.
        var context = new List<string>();
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.ProjectTitle))          context.Add(p.ProjectTitle);
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle)) context.Add(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle!);
        context.Add(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.MentorNames) ? "ללא מנחה" : $"מנחה: {p.MentorNames}");

        return new TeamItem(
            ProjectId:  p.ProjectId,
            TeamName:   string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.TeamName) ? p.ProjectTitle : p.TeamName!,
            Context:    string.Join(" · ", context),
            Reason:     reason,
            Tone:       atRisk ? MStatusDot.DotTone.Rose : MStatusDot.DotTone.Violet,
            ReasonTone: atRisk ? MRow.RowMetaTone.Rose  : MRow.RowMetaTone.Default,
            IsMine:     p.IsSupervisedByCurrentUser);
    }

    // ── 3. מועדים קרובים ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private sealed record UpcomingItem(string When, string KindClass, string Label,
                                       string Href, DateTime Date);

    /// <summary>
    /// The course's next milestone deadlines, floored at today, grouped so one
    /// deadline is one row.
    ///
    /// <para>TODAY IS THE FLOOR, applied at the source. Nothing is lost: an
    /// overdue milestone is already the business of the team rows above, and
    /// /lecturer/calendar still renders every past event — this filter is local
    /// to this card's view-model and touches no query, endpoint or DTO.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>ONE ROW PER (MILESTONE, DATE). A group of one still names its
    /// team, so nothing is hidden — the row simply says "5 צוותים" when there
    /// are five.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<UpcomingItem> UpcomingItems
    {
        get
        {
            var today = DateTime.Today;

            return CourseTeams
                .Where(p => p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate is { } d && d.Date >= today)
                .GroupBy(p => new
                {
                    Date  = p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate!.Value.Date,
                    Title = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle)
                                ? "" : p.CurrentMilestoneTitle!,
                })
                .OrderBy(g => g.Key.Date)
                .Take(UpcomingPreview)
                .Select(g =>
                {
                    var first = g.First();
                    int n     = g.Count();

                    // The tile bar says WHAT sort of deadline this is, not how
                    // urgent it is — a group takes the strongest thing anything
                    // in it is waiting on.
                    string kindClass = g.Any(p => p.MissingSubmissionCount > 0) ? "mdash-kind-submission"
                                     : g.Any(p => p.OpenRequestCount      > 0) ? "mdash-kind-review"
                                     :                                            "mdash-kind-milestone";

                    string label = g.Key.Title.Length > 0
                        ? g.Key.Title
                        : (n == 1 ? first.ProjectTitle : "אבן דרך");

                    string meta = n == 1
                        ? Join(WhenLabel(g.Key.Date), OneOf(first.TeamName, first.ProjectTitle))
                        : Join(WhenLabel(g.Key.Date), $"{n} צוותים");

                    // One team → its workspace. Many → the calendar, which is
                    // the screen that can show them all.
                    string href = n == 1
                        ? $"projects/{first.ProjectId}/overview"
                        : "lecturer/calendar";

                    return new UpcomingItem(meta, kindClass, label, href, g.Key.Date);
                })
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    private static string WhenLabel(DateTime d)
    {
        int days = (d.Date - DateTime.Today).Days;
        return days == 0            ? "היום"
             : days == 1            ? "מחר"
             : days is > 1 and <= 7 ? $"עוד {days} ימים"
             : d.ToString("d/M", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    }

    // ── Copy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// HEBREW COUNTS ONE THING DIFFERENTLY FROM MANY, and these two lines are
    /// the ones a preview cap can force to "1".
    ///
    /// <para>"1 משימות נוספות" and "ועוד 1 צוותים" are a numeral in front of a
    /// plural noun. Hebrew puts the number after the singular noun instead,
    /// and for "one more" it drops the numeral entirely. The count is only ever
    /// ≥ 1 here: both call sites are guarded by <c>Count &gt; Preview</c>.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Stated identically on Mentor Home, which draws the same two lines
    /// from its own lists. Two copies rather than one shared helper because the
    /// second line's noun differs — the mentor previews teams, this previews
    /// teams that need attention — and a helper taking the noun as a parameter
    /// would be a worse home for the rule than the sentence itself.</para></summary>
    private static string MoreTasksLabel(int n) =>
        n == 1 ? "+ משימה אחת נוספת" : $"+ {n} משימות נוספות";

    private static string MoreTeamsLabel(int n) =>
        n == 1 ? "ועוד צוות אחד שדורש תשומת לב" : $"ועוד {n} צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב";

    private static string OneOf(string? first, string? second) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(first)    ? first!.Trim()
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(second) ? second!.Trim()
        : "";

    /// <summary>Join the parts that are actually present, so a row with no
    /// mentor has a shorter context line rather than a string of separators.</summary>
    private static string Join(params string?[] parts) =>
        string.Join(" · ", parts.Where(v => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(v)).Select(v => v!.Trim()));

    private static string? MentorLabel(string? names) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(names) ? null : $"מנחה: {names.Trim()}";

    /// <summary>
    /// A request's type, IN HEBREW OR NOT AT ALL.
    ///
    /// <para><c>RequestTypes.Label</c> passes an unknown type through verbatim,
    /// which is right for a screen that must not silently drop a value — but
    /// live and seeded rows carry types outside the Shared constant list, so an
    /// unguarded call prints "ScopeChange" in the middle of a Hebrew line. A
    /// context line is an aid, not a record: when there is no Hebrew word the
    /// row omits the type, and the requests screen still shows it.</para></summary>
    private static string? TypeName(string type) =>
        RequestTypes.All.Contains(type) ? RequestTypes.Label(type) : null;

    /// <summary>
    /// How long a request has been open, in browser-local calendar days.
    ///
    /// <para><c>ProjectRequestRowDto</c> carries no server-side waiting age —
    /// only submissions do, via <c>DaysWaiting</c> — so this mirrors
    /// LecturerTasksPage.DaysOpen exactly. It is compared against
    /// <c>MentorAttention.AgeOf</c>, the single shared threshold, and against
    /// nothing else. The durable fix is a server-computed WaitingDays on the
    /// request row, which is a server change this pass does not make.</para></summary>
    private static int DaysOpen(ProjectRequestRowDto r) =>
        Math.Max(0, (int)(DateTime.Now.Date - r.CreatedAt.ToLocalTime().Date).TotalDays);

    // ── WHAT USED TO BE HERE: a page-local WaitingLabel(int) ─────────────────
    //
    // Four Hebrew strings ("ממתינה היום" … "ממתינה N ימים") reimplementing
    // MentorAging.ShortLabel, which is Shared and already documented as "the
    // compact form, for a scannable list row" — exactly what a tag needs. The
    // queue now calls that directly, so the mentor's Home and the lecturer's
    // say a wait in the same words, from one place.
    //
    // A WAIT, NEVER "באיחור", is that helper's own rule and the reason it is
    // the right one to borrow: neither a request nor a pending mentor approval
    // has a deadline it could be late for. The only "באיחור" left on this page
    // is DueLabel's, on personal tasks, which do carry a real DueDate.
}
